# Test Patterns

## Builder — dedicated class, never static fixtures

The `Builder` is a **class** (not a collection of functions or fixtures) instantiated per test with the test `AsyncSession`. It owns all entity creation logic.

```python
# builder.py
class Builder:
    def __init__(self, session: AsyncSession) -> None:
        self.session = session

    async def build_order(
        self,
        *,
        title: str = "Test Order",
        status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.NEW,
        user_id: UUID | None = None,
    ) -> OrderModel:
        result = await self.session.execute(
            insert(OrderModel)
            .values(id=uuid.uuid4(), title=title, status=status, user_id=user_id or uuid.uuid4())
            .returning(OrderModel)
        )
        order = result.scalar_one()
        await self.session.flush()
        return order

    async def build_order_file(self, *, order_id: UUID, status: FileStatus = FileStatus.DONE) -> OrderFileModel:
        ...

    # Cached default — created once per test
    @cached_property
    async def default_order(self) -> OrderModel:
        return await self.build_order(title="Default Order")
```

```python
# ❌ Never — static fixture with hardcoded data
@pytest.fixture
def order():
    return {"id": "...", "title": "test"}

# ✅ Always — Builder in test
async def test_get_order(client, builder, bearer_headers):
    order = await builder.build_order(title="My Order", status=OrderStatus.NEW)
    response = await client.get(f"/api/v1/orders/{order.id}", headers=bearer_headers())
    assert response.status_code == 200
    assert response.json()["title"] == "My Order"
```

## Test Naming Convention

`test_returns_<STATUS>_when_<CONDITION>`

```python
async def test_returns_200_when_order_exists(...)
async def test_returns_404_when_order_not_found(...)
async def test_returns_403_when_user_lacks_permission(...)
async def test_returns_200_when_file_queued_for_s3_upload(...)  # not 202
```

## Test Organization (classes per endpoint/usecase)

```python
class TestGetOrder:
    async def test_returns_200_when_order_exists(self, client, builder, bearer_headers): ...
    async def test_returns_404_when_order_not_found(self, client, bearer_headers): ...

class TestCreateOrder:
    async def test_returns_201_on_success(self, client, bearer_headers): ...
    async def test_returns_422_when_title_empty(self, client, bearer_headers): ...
```

## Asserting Kafka (FakeKafkaBroker API)

```python
# FakeKafkaBroker is injected into DI container at session scope
messages = fake_kafka.get_messages_for_topic("storage.s3.order.upload")
assert len(messages) == 1

# Predicate-based assertion
assert fake_kafka.was_message_published(
    "storage.s3.order.upload",
    predicate=lambda m: m.get("content_type") == "application/pdf",
)
fake_kafka.clear_published()  # reset between subtests if needed
```

## Asserting S3 (MockS3Client API)

```python
assert mock_s3.was_operation_performed("put_object", key="examples/...")
assert mock_s3.get_uploaded_content("my/key") == b"expected bytes"
put_ops = mock_s3.get_operations_by_type("put_object")
```

## conftest isolation mechanism

```
Each test:
  connection.begin()                         ← outer transaction
    AsyncSession(join_transaction_mode=      ← UseCase's session.commit()
      "create_savepoint")                       creates a SAVEPOINT, not a real commit
    _current_db_session.set(session)         ← TestSessionProvider reads this
    [test runs here]
  transaction.rollback()                     ← outer transaction rolls back → DB clean
```

## Rules

- No real Kafka, S3, Redis calls in tests — FakeKafkaBroker / MockS3Client / MockRefreshTokenStore
- Each test is isolated via `join_transaction_mode="create_savepoint"` (not `begin_nested`)
- One test file per endpoint or use case
- `bearer_headers(role="admin")` — factory from conftest, creates valid JWT
- Group related tests in classes, not loose functions

