# shared/ — What Belongs There

`backend/shared/` contains code used by **multiple domains** or at the **application level**. Never put domain-specific logic here.

| Location | Content |
|----------|---------|
| `shared/settings/` | App config dataclasses, YAML loaders, `load_settings()` |
| `shared/di/` | Dishka providers — `AppProvider`, `SessionProvider`, domain providers |
| `shared/kafka_streams/` | `KafkaProducerWrapper`, `@kafka_subscriber`, topics, S3 event helpers |
| `storage/pg/` | `Database`, `Base` — one engine for all domains |
| `storage/redis/` | `RedisClient` — shared cache/session store |
| `storage/s3/` | `S3Client` — used by Kafka consumers |

Single-domain code stays in `backend/app/<domain>/`. Cross-domain utilities (pagination helpers, date utils, etc.) go to `shared/utils/`.
